// Test: bugfixes/sem014_capability_default_uses_unknown_member
// Changed in 0.33.186: this. is not part of Clean (developer decision); the
//   default body names the member by its bare name
// Grammar: can_declaration, can_default_body
// Semantic: SEM014 — a default body may name members of the claiming class
//   only to call methods of its own capability; `color` is not part of
//   Describe (the semantic-rules.md §SEM014 example)
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.184
// Expected output:
// Expected error:
//   SEM014
//   The default body of 'Describe.tag' uses 'color', but 'color' is not a method of capability 'Describe'
//
// Regression: the example compiled with no error.

start:
	print("test")

can Describe:
	string describe()
	string tag()
		return color                 // ERROR: color is not part of Describe
